.TH XD\-DESK 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-desk \- Display Properties
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-desk
.OP \-\-page n
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-desk
is Display Properties (Control Panel > Display), with Windows XP's tabs,
Windows 2000's Effects, and one for what only Linux has:
.TP
.B Themes
A theme sets the visual style, the wallpaper, the sound scheme and the
mouse pointers together, as XP's did: Windows XP and Windows Classic,
and the installed theme packages that bring a wallpaper, sounds or
pointers (see
.IR docs/THEMES.md ),
with a sample of the desktop. A theme changed in the other tabs shows as
"(Modified)". Save As... saves the current settings as a theme package
(.xdtheme), Delete moves one of the user's own to the Trash, and
Browse... (the list's last item) installs a package or converts a Windows
theme (.theme), its wallpaper, sounds and pointers with it, with
.BR xd\-theme\-import .
.TP
.B Desktop
The wallpaper and how it is placed (Windows 2000's Background).
.TP
.B Screen Saver
The screen saver, its settings and a preview, the Wait, Password protected,
and when to turn the monitors off.
.TP
.B Appearance
The visual style (Classic, Luna, Watercolor or Aero), colour scheme and
font size, with a preview; Advanced Appearance, the scheme item by item;
in Aero, Windows 7's window colours.
The installed theme packages follow the styles, with their colours and
sizes; Browse... installs a package (.xdtheme) or converts a Windows
visual style (.msstyles or .theme) with
.BR xd\-theme\-import .
.TP
.B Effects
Menu and tooltip transitions, large icons, dragging windows as an
outline, hiding underlined letters until Alt is pressed, and font
smoothing: antialiasing, subpixel order and hinting, which a real session
also gives other programs (GNOME's settings and GTK's settings.ini);
and how theme packages' images are scaled for high DPI.
.TP
.B Settings
Each monitor's position, resolution, refresh rate, scale and orientation,
or turning it off; Identify shows each monitor's number on it.
Advanced opens the monitor's properties: on its Monitor tab the screen
refresh rate and Variable refresh rate, which lets full-screen games
change the refresh rate to match their frame rate (off by default, since
some monitors flicker with it; grey when the monitor or its graphics
adapter can't).
New display settings revert after 15 seconds unless kept.
.TP
.B Linux
The icon theme, and the GTK and Qt styles of other programs.
Night Light... makes the screen warmer at night: its strength (1700 to
4700 K), and all the time, from sunset to sunrise (at a place GeoClue
finds, or typed in as latitude and longitude) or between set hours.
Color Management... opens
.BR xd\-color (1).
.PP
Apply and OK write
.IR desktop.ini ,
which the compositor, the shell and the other programs follow at once.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-page " n"
Open on tab
.IR n ,
from 0 (Themes) to 6 (Linux): 1 Desktop, 2 Screen Saver, 3 Appearance,
4 Effects, 5 Settings. The default is 0 (Themes), as XP's desk.cpl.
.TP
.BI \-\-style " style"
.TQ
.BI \-\-scheme " file"
The visual style and colour scheme of the dialog instead of those in
.IR desktop.ini .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xeondesktop/desktop.ini
.BR [Appearance] ,
.BR [Desktop] ,
.BR [Wallpaper] ,
.BR [Effects] ,
.BR [CustomScheme] ,
.BR [ScreenSaver] ,
.B [ScreenSaver.*]
and
.BR [NightLight] .
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xeondesktop/monitors.ini
The monitors' settings.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xeondesktop/sounds.ini
The sound scheme, which a theme may set.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/xeondesktop/theme-files/
.TQ
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/icons/xdtheme-*/
A theme's wallpaper and sounds, and its pointers, unpacked when it is
chosen.
.TP
.I /usr/share/xeondesktop/schemes/
The colour schemes.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/xeondesktop/themes/
.TQ
.I /usr/share/xeondesktop/themes/
Theme packages: folders or .xdtheme files. Browse... installs into the
first.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-compositor (1),
.BR xd\-color (1),
.BR xd\-lock (1),
.BR xd\-control (1)
